        <body>
            <div xml:id="d202">

                <pb facs="0350" n="238" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg238"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Schuyler to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-12-20"><hi rendition="#italic">December 20,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 600.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your telegrams of November 6
                    and December 14, concerning the project for the complete neutralization of the
                        <pb facs="0351" n="239" xml:id="pg239"/> railways of Manchuria, I have the
                    honor to inform you that in compliance with the instructions in the latter
                    telegram I handed to the minister for foreign affairs, Mr. Iswolsky, a formal
                    note, with accompanying aide-mémoire, embodying the views of the Department of
                    State as set forth in the telegram of November 6, regarding the neutralization
                    project. Copies of the note and aide-mémoire are inclosed herewith for your
                    information. Mr. Iswolsky read over the aide-mémoire very carefully in my
                    presence and then remarked that he was a little disappointed that the whole
                    matter had not been, worked out in detail, but that he would give the project
                    his careful consideration.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Montgomery
                    Schuyler.</hi></signed></closer>



